  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc. We've established that (a) multiprofile is a major gain over singleprofile (+0.13), (b) scvi_n200 beats pca_n2000, and (c) transformer vs avgpool aggregation makes negligible difference (~0.003). Uncertainty: We have not tested whether scgpt, a fundamentally different RNA representation (autoregressive generative model vs VAE), could outperform scvi_n200 in the multiprofile setting. This experiment isolates the RNA encoder effect while holding the proven multiprofile + transformer pipeline constant. Rationale: With 4 experiments remaining, establishing the best RNA-only baseline is critical before investing in multimodal fusion (which adds complexity and the image modality alone was very weak at 0.21). If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, it opens a new encoder direction; if not, we confirm scvi_n200 as optimal and can focus remaining budget on testing whether multimodal fusion adds value on top of the best RNA-only config."
}

